{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791282128,"nonce":"LTytdXWYx3wErVzB+gqBD0g3y2w=","title":"Type.createEnum copies Dynamic parameter boxes into typed enum fields","message":"Issue4407 passes a Dynamic enum type to Type.createEnum with `untyped [null, \"123\"]`. The type lookup and constructor name succeed, but create_enum_value copies each Array\u003cDynamic\u003e slot directly into the enum payload. The first slot contains a boxed null where Null\u003cInt\u003e expects a null pointer; the second contains a boxed String where the enum field expects a HaxeString pointer. Type.enumEq therefore reports false against an equivalent direct constructor. Normalize each parameter according to the registered enum field type while creating the value.\n\nComplete tiered gate at 95f60485: 842/1094. With the change: 843/1094; Issue4407 gained PASS and no rows changed status otherwise. The wider Dynamic Type API and Int64 questions remain tracked in d5a05c2; this issue covers the enum parameter representation only.","files":null}]}